[The most clearly and robustly supported decision→goal connections. Name the decisions and goals in plain language. Convey connection strength with words — "clearly advances", "strongly supports", "directly enables" — never with numbers or tier labels.]

## Coverage and Orphans
[How much of the decision activity is accounted for by goals, and which decisions appear disconnected from any goal. Use proportional language ("most", "about half", "a handful", "several") — never raw counts pulled from any table or list.]

## Tensions and Synergies
[Where decisions pull in competing directions relative to goals, and where they reinforce each other. Name specific decisions and goals involved. If none are present, say so plainly.]

## Gaps and Cautions
[The weakest or most uncertain connections, missing coverage areas, and what a reader should be cautious about when interpreting this briefing.]

